D.J.Hayes already mentioned that an old version of Nethack often
gave Wizards an athame as starting equipment.

Checking the source, regular liches and demiliches never get athames.
Master liches can get one.  Archliches can get one and sometimes it
is rustproofed.  Other than them, athames are like runeswords in
that you can wish for one but they never appear randomly.  For that
matter, the fedora is the same way.

> Why would you want to score an athame anyway?  By the time you're tangling 
> with liches you already have a better artifact weapon, right?

Athames engrave any number of letters in one turn vs other methods
that engrave one letter per turn.  Big difference with the E word.
Maybe big enough that it unbalanced Wizard class and that's why
the DevTeam changed to initial equipment of Wizards.  Also where
most blades write in the dust athames engrave in the stone floor.
For a well kitted character with wishes to burn, a blessed +3
rustproof athame is an endgame luxury item.  For an early Wizard
this advantage of athames makes them survivable.

For regular combat purposes, athames are identical in damage and
weight to regular daggers.  So they are better than orcish daggers
but both elven daggers and silver daggers are better than athames.

